{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01542VQauREesHb8FtYZ5xHk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 1–2: Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations diverge on edge cases. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go implementations), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (cross-platform syscall wrappers), `pkg/format/` (shared formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets, excluded from generation).\n\n**Current state:** All packages in releases 00.0–01.3 have generated implementations at tagged commits (4,586 LOC across 22 files): `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/version`, `cmd/wc`, `cmd/cat`, `cmd/sponge`, `cmd/du`. The working branch contains specifications only; `code_status` shows all use cases as \"not started\" on this branch.\n\n**Current releases:** 00.0 (foundational infra), 01.0 (wc), 01.1 (cat), 01.2 (sponge), 01.3 (du).\n\n## Step 3: Priority Reasoning\n\nAll packages in releases 00.0–01.3 exist in `source_code` and must not be recreated. However, there is a clear architectural gap: **pkg/sys lists \"Signal handling (SIGPIPE, SIGHUP, SIGWINCH)\" as a required capability** but the source code for pkg/sys contains only `terminal.go` and `fileinfo*.go` — no signal handling. Meanwhile, three cmd/ packages duplicate signal handling code:\n\n- `cmd/cat/main.go:166-172` — `installSIGPIPEHandler()` (exits 0 on SIGPIPE)\n- `cmd/du/main.go:215-222` — `installSIGPIPEHandler()` (exits 0 on SIGPIPE)\n- `cmd/sponge/main.go:338-346` — `installCleanupHandler()` (cleanup + exit 1 on SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP/SIGPIPE)\n\nThis duplication violates SC4 (\"no duplication of syscall or formatting code across cmd/ packages\"). The shared signal handling belongs in pkg/sys per the architecture. This maps to release 00.0 (uc003-sys) and enables releases 01.1 (cat), 01.2 (sponge), and 01.3 (du).\n\n## Steps 4–5: Proposed Task\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/sys: Add signal handling functions (prd006 R5.4, prd007 R1.5, prd009 R5.1)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd002-sys.yaml (pkg/sys PRD -- find signal handling requirements)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/sys component -- lists \"Signal handling (SIGPIPE, SIGHUP, SIGWINCH)\" as a required capability)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo.go (existing package structure, copyright header, doc comment conventions)\n      - pkg/sys/terminal.go (existing package pattern for single-purpose source files)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/signal.go\n        action: create\n        note: Exported SIGPIPE handler and cleanup signal handler functions\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement an exported InstallSIGPIPEHandler function in pkg/sys that registers a SIGPIPE signal handler. When SIGPIPE is received, the handler exits the process with code 0. This consolidates the duplicated SIGPIPE handlers required by prd006-cat R5.4 and prd009-du R5.1 into the shared library.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement an exported InstallCleanupHandler function in pkg/sys that accepts a cleanup callback (func()) and registers signal handlers for SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP, and SIGPIPE. When any of these signals is received, the handler runs the cleanup callback (if non-nil) then exits with code 1. This consolidates the cleanup handler required by prd007-sponge R1.5 into the shared library.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Both handler functions must use Go's os/signal.Notify with a buffered channel of capacity 1 and a background goroutine that blocks on channel receive. This is the standard Go signal handling pattern and matches the conventions in existing pkg/sys code.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"File named signal.go in pkg/sys -- derived from the architecture capability name 'Signal handling (SIGPIPE, SIGHUP, SIGWINCH)' listed under the pkg/sys component in ARCHITECTURE.yaml.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"InstallSIGPIPEHandler takes no parameters and exits with code 0. InstallCleanupHandler takes a func() parameter and exits with code 1 after calling it. These signatures match the two distinct signal handling patterns used across cmd/ utilities: broken-pipe tolerance (exit 0) and resource cleanup on termination (exit 1).\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/sys/signal.go exists with exported InstallSIGPIPEHandler and InstallCleanupHandler functions.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Code compiles as part of package sys with no errors (go build ./pkg/sys/).\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"File includes copyright header (matching pkg/sys/fileinfo.go), SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT, and doc comments with Implements: references to the prd002-sys requirement IDs found in the PRD.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":104731,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10b7607d-93ff-47cf-ad76-a0a477c17b5a","uuid":"cf7c0703-7f08-439c-b26a-394661201606"}
